 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? You' not alone. Orange is tough skin to beat. A few tips. start with clean skin, no grime or oil. Then exfoliate if your skin feels rough. Now mix your tone powder with a little bit of the base liquid so it flows smoothly. Starting on the shadow side helps. Yes, light skin needs less base so it stays fresh longer. Dark skin needs more base to prevent stripes. Use a thick brush for dark skin. Yes, mix it up so the pigment is evenly scattered. Then apply it in thin layers, each one fully dry before the next. Hold the brush at quarter inch depth Then build up the shadows under the eyes. A thin thin line around the eyes and a bit on the cheekbones can make you pop.",
